WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:02.500
Could Lucifer lose his immortality?

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:05.510
Will Ella uncover the devil's secret?

00:00:05.510 --> 00:00:08.160
And who will end up ruler of Hell by the end
of the series?

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:13.469
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video we're investigating 15 incredible

00:00:13.469 --> 00:00:17.320
yet possible theories and predictions that
could change everything for the final two

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:18.439
seasons of Lucifer.

00:00:18.439 --> 00:00:21.359
We'll be talking spoilers, so take care if
you're not caught up.

00:00:21.359 --> 00:00:22.550
"This is gonna be good."

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:23.980
"Yeah, I'll have some of that."

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:28.949
A big moment in the first part of Season 5
comes when Lucifer regains his invulnerability

00:00:28.949 --> 00:00:29.949
around Chloe.

00:00:29.949 --> 00:00:35.000
Dan shoots the Devil with Chloe nearby, but
Lucifer emerges unscathed and rather pleased

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:39.410
with the outcome, even offering himself up
as a "Devil Shield" to the Detective.

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:43.899
But there was an important moment earlier
in Season 5 that suggests this development

00:00:43.899 --> 00:00:48.520
could go into reverse, with Lucifer choosing
to forsake his invulnerability entirely to

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:50.020
become a mortal being.

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:55.300
In the noir episode, Lilith gives up her immortality
breathing into her ring that she gives Lucifer,

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:59.160
and explains an insight she's gleaned from
her thousands of years living among humans:

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.730
"They all think they want to live forever.

00:01:01.730 --> 00:01:04.710
But they already have something so much more
precious.

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:05.710
It's knowing there's an end.

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:07.520
That's what makes the rest of it count.

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:10.000
That's what connects them to one another."

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:15.350
Likewise in season 3 we heard Cain, aka Marcus
Pierce, compare immortality to hell:

00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:17.670
"I've walked this Earth for thousands of years.

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:20.079
I have seen everything, I have done everything."

00:01:20.079 --> 00:01:21.750
It's almost like you're in..."

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:22.750
"Hell?

00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:23.750
Yeah!"

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:26.760
Now that Lucifer and Chloe are a couple, what
could be worse for Lucifer than watching Chloe

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:30.960
eventually die and then continuing to live
for an eternity without her.

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:35.649
Back in 1946 when Lilith asked Lucifer if
he'd ever made an emotional connection with

00:01:35.649 --> 00:01:37.450
a human, Luci scoffed at the notion.

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:38.450
"Ha!

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:40.330
It would take a literal miracle for me to
want something like that,

00:01:40.330 --> 00:01:42.990
and I'm fairly certain my father's not handing
those out anymore."

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:47.850
But of course that did happen, so could Lucifer
decide to follow Lilith's example and give

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:51.830
up his own immortality, so that he and Chloe
can grow old together?

00:01:51.830 --> 00:01:55.000
Or, alternatively, could Chloe become immortal
from the ring?

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:57.680
But then, what about Trixie?

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:01.619
Another outcome that could solve all that
is Lucifer being forgiven for his rebellion

00:02:01.619 --> 00:02:04.430
and being able to return to the Silver City
when he wishes,

00:02:04.430 --> 00:02:08.789
so that when Chloe eventually dies, they can
be together there as well.

00:02:08.789 --> 00:02:13.880
In Season 5, while Luci returns to earth to
deal with Michael, Amenadiel takes his place

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:16.070
in Hell to keep the demons in check.

00:02:16.070 --> 00:02:20.710
But to Lucifer's surprise, in the fifth episode,
he discovers Amenadiel's back with Linda,

00:02:20.710 --> 00:02:25.120
and when Luci demands to know why he's left
Hell unguarded, Amenadiel explains:

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:27.880
"There I was...
wandering the corridors of Hell, when...

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:28.970
I heard a voice.

00:02:28.970 --> 00:02:31.550
A voice that I never expected to hear in Hell."

00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:35.880
According to Amenadiel, that voice was God
who told him that Hell no longer needed a

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:36.880
warden.

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:40.440
When I first saw this scene, it struck me
as odd, given that having a proper ruler watching

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:44.600
over the Underworld was such an important
plot point for Season 4.

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:48.570
And given that Amenadiel says he thought that
it was strange to hear God's voice in Hell,

00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:53.260
I wonder whether Michael sneaked into Hell
and impersonated God's voice to fool Amenadiel

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:56.150
into leaving the Underworld without a ruler
again.

00:02:56.150 --> 00:03:01.100
This could be yet another trick Michael has
pulled to make Luci look bad in front of their

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:02.100
father.

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:05.940
We know Michael can easily switch accents
and we already saw him performing this trick

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:10.890
on Dan when he called his phone pretending
to be Lucifer so that Dan would see Luci's

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:11.930
devil face.

00:03:11.930 --> 00:03:17.590
Now that Dan's discovered Lucifer's true identity,
out of the main cast only Ella is still unware

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:19.570
that Luci is literally the devil.

00:03:19.570 --> 00:03:24.430
However, I expect that will change when she
finally finds out by the end of Season 5.

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:28.370
And given Ella's religious beliefs, I think
this moment could be an even bigger shock

00:03:28.370 --> 00:03:31.260
for her than it was for Chloe or Dan or Linda.

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:35.210
Ella says she grew up among criminals and
dirt bags, but that when she turned to God,

00:03:35.210 --> 00:03:37.040
it set her on a better path.

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:41.040
So her reaction when she finds out she's been
living alongside the Devil as his friend in

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:43.100
LA will be very interesting.

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:47.550
Of course, this isn't the first time Ella's
unwittingly befriended a celestial, as her

00:03:47.550 --> 00:03:51.310
ghost friend Ray-Ray was actually Luci's angel
sister Azrael.

00:03:51.310 --> 00:03:56.400
Ella also has this dark side to her which
the show played up a lot more in Season 5

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:59.050
with her attraction to what she calls "bad
guys".

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:03.590
And then there was Pete, the seemingly nice
guy secret serial killer, who also said he

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:04.890
saw darkness in Ella.

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:09.490
And there was a very interesting moment in
the ¡Diablo! episode when Ella finds a prop

00:04:09.490 --> 00:04:12.690
weapon
"supposed to be the only blade that can kill

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:15.340
the Devil"
and then proceeds to attack Lucifer with the

00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:17.290
rubber knife.

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:18.290
"Hi-ya!

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:20.690
"Sorry, that seemed a lot funnier in my head."

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:21.690
"I'm sure."

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:25.070
Now, obviously the moment is played for laughs
here, but it could also be a little bit of

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:29.750
foreshadowing for Ella trying to attack the
Devil when she discovers him on Earth?

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:34.060
By the end of the series, I expect we will
find someone in charge of Hell who isn't Lucifer,

00:04:34.060 --> 00:04:38.500
as I think God will at some point recognise
that he's done enough to serve out his punishment.

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:43.290
The most likely candidate at this point is
Michael, because once his dastardly schemes

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:47.260
against Lucifer are revealed to God,
he would surely get banished from Heaven,

00:04:47.260 --> 00:04:50.430
and perhaps sent to the Underworld to rule
in Lucifer's place.

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:55.060
A possible, though less obvious, option for
new ruler of Hell would be Maze.

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:59.650
She was already keen to go back to Hell in
Season 1, but Lucifer insisted they stay in

00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:03.030
LA and so she decided to find a purpose for
herself as a bounty hunter.

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:08.160
And at the start of season 5, Maze is mad
at Luci for going down to Hell without her.

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:13.340
The technical problem with Maze taking over
down under is that she's a demon, so theoretically

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:17.120
it would break this rule:
"Hell was built so that no demon could take

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:18.321
control of the throne.

00:05:18.321 --> 00:05:19.660
Only a celestial could rule."

00:05:19.660 --> 00:05:23.630
But given everything that happens in the show,
it's not impossible for this rule to be broken

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:26.730
if the writers wanted to make it work.

00:05:26.730 --> 00:05:31.060
Something that could play into this is Maze
discovering that she isn't an ordinary demon

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:32.740
and does actually have a soul.

00:05:32.740 --> 00:05:37.460
In fact, there was a hint to this in the "Mr
and Mrs Mazikeen Smith" episode of Season

00:05:37.460 --> 00:05:39.600
3:
"When you kill, you lose a piece of your soul.

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:41.430
I get the feeling you understand that."

00:05:41.430 --> 00:05:42.430
"Sorry.

00:05:42.430 --> 00:05:43.430
No soul here."

00:05:43.430 --> 00:05:44.430
"That's not what I see."

00:05:44.430 --> 00:05:48.680
My other theory is that Maze will resolve
her existential angst via the ring her mother

00:05:48.680 --> 00:05:53.880
Lilith gave Lucifer, and I go into detail
about that in my Ending Explained video.

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:57.880
Maze is such a fan favourite that I expect
she'll eventually find her soulmate by the

00:05:57.880 --> 00:05:58.880
end of the series.

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:03.480
[At the moment] Eve seems like the best option
for Maze as they already formed a connection

00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:06.930
in Season 4,
and if Maze is also in charge of Hell, then

00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:11.550
I can definitely see Eve joining her there
as she enjoyed helping Luci punish sinners

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:15.290
when she was with him on Earth,
and then Kinley also suggested Eve could be

00:06:15.290 --> 00:06:18.520
Queen of Hell with Lucifer, so why not with
Maze instead?

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:22.850
A character who might not make it out of the
series alive is Dan, though he could still

00:06:22.850 --> 00:06:26.510
get a happy ending of sorts reuniting with
Charlotte in Heaven.

00:06:26.510 --> 00:06:30.730
In the first episode of Season 5, we see that
despite his attempts to be positive, Dan is

00:06:30.730 --> 00:06:34.050
still struggling to get over Charlotte's death
from Season 3.

00:06:34.050 --> 00:06:38.320
I think he will get a special moment to shine
before the end of the series,

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:42.580
perhaps playing a crucial part in defeating
Michael as Lucifer saw an unusual strength

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:47.130
in Dan when he was wielding the powerful divine
weapon Azrael's Blade in Season 2:

00:06:47.130 --> 00:06:51.200
"You're fighting the blade, which indicates
a strength I didn't know you had."

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:56.000
If Michael was able to send Amenadiel into
a fear spiral that made his time manipulation

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:59.400
powers go crazy,
could it be possible that Michael's fear mojo

00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:04.470
was also to blame for that mysterious moment
in Season 4 when Lucifer's mojo powers went

00:07:04.470 --> 00:07:05.470
haywire?

00:07:05.470 --> 00:07:09.760
At the time, Lucifer's self-hatred and fear
that Chloe couldn't accept him for who he

00:07:09.760 --> 00:07:13.340
truly was, meant he began transforming physically
into his full devil form,

00:07:13.340 --> 00:07:18.090
but a side effect was that everyone in Lux
began to tell him what they desired, even

00:07:18.090 --> 00:07:20.060
though he wasn't asking them.

00:07:20.060 --> 00:07:24.430
Michael seems to like lurking in the shadows,
hidden from view, and in Season 5, there was

00:07:24.430 --> 00:07:27.780
that moment where he vanishes into the crowd
at Lux.

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:32.540
Indeed Lucifer also commented that Michael
enjoys hiding himself away.

00:07:32.540 --> 00:07:36.620
"If past is prologue, he's probably hidden
himself off somewhere to laugh about the mess

00:07:36.620 --> 00:07:37.620
he's made..."

00:07:37.620 --> 00:07:41.340
So, perhaps Michael has been around longer
than we know, causing havoc and triggering

00:07:41.340 --> 00:07:44.480
events like Lucifer's mojo going wrong in
Season 4.

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:50.680
After all, he did tell Lucifer that he's basically
been manipulating him since the dawn of time.

00:07:50.680 --> 00:07:53.970
Something which is still a mystery about Michael
is the reason for his slopey shoulder, as

00:07:53.970 --> 00:07:55.130
Lucifer calls it.

00:07:55.130 --> 00:07:59.781
I expect the backstory to this will be revealed
in the second part of Season 5, and it may

00:07:59.781 --> 00:08:03.440
be an injury he suffered during Luci's rebellion
against God.

00:08:03.440 --> 00:08:07.150
If Lucifer does have anything to do with it,
then of course it will be yet another of Michael's

00:08:07.150 --> 00:08:09.470
grievances towards his brother.

00:08:09.470 --> 00:08:13.871
The moment many Deckerstar fans waited five
seasons for finally happened when Lucifer

00:08:13.871 --> 00:08:17.780
and Chloe did the deed and discovered that
Hell didn't freeze over.

00:08:17.780 --> 00:08:21.160
But what are the chances that Chloe could
now be pregnant with Lucifer's child?

00:08:21.160 --> 00:08:25.830
It already happened to Amenadiel and Linda
on the show and Lucifer even joked about it

00:08:25.830 --> 00:08:29.419
when Chloe found herself naked in Lucifer's
bed in the first season:

00:08:29.419 --> 00:08:31.670
"I'm pretty sure we made Rosemary's baby."

00:08:31.670 --> 00:08:36.130
I don't think this will be a main plot point
as it could feel like too much of a repeat

00:08:36.130 --> 00:08:39.830
of Charlie's storyline, and it's not something
I'm keen to see myself;

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:43.330
however, there are fans who would like this,
so it could be something that happens at the

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:48.360
very end of the series as a kind of epilogue,
if Lucifer and Chloe settle down together.

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:51.890
Speaking of which, it's entirely possible
we'll see the devilish couple tie the knot

00:08:51.890 --> 00:08:53.910
before the show's over.

00:08:53.910 --> 00:08:58.240
The "¡Diablo!" episode is packed with many
comical meta moments as Lucifer and Chloe

00:08:58.240 --> 00:09:02.580
investigate a murder on a TV show inspired
by their own partnership.

00:09:02.580 --> 00:09:07.350
During the case, Lucifer chances upon a script
for an unaired episode called "Diablo in Space".

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:11.940
And when he and Dan act out the script, they
read out the line "A devil in the heavens"

00:09:11.940 --> 00:09:16.360
which makes me wonder if we can look forward
to a Lucifer episode that's actually set in

00:09:16.360 --> 00:09:17.360
Heaven.

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:21.089
And I go into lots more detail about that
hilarious episode, including all the little

00:09:21.089 --> 00:09:24.890
easter eggs and references, in my Season 5
Things You Missed video.

00:09:24.890 --> 00:09:28.850
Tap the card here or follow the link in the
video description.

00:09:28.850 --> 00:09:33.810
Perhaps the upcoming musical episode titled
"Bloody Celestial Karaoke Jam" will end up

00:09:33.810 --> 00:09:38.620
taking place in Heaven, where we'll get to
meet another of Lucifer's siblings Castiel.

00:09:38.620 --> 00:09:43.820
When Remy arrived on Earth in Season 4, Amenadiel
made reference to Castiel's love of song,

00:09:43.820 --> 00:09:47.250
so it feels like this will be the appropriate
episode to introduce the character.

00:09:47.250 --> 00:09:50.000
"So, what brings you to Earth?
you need a break from Castiel singing?"

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:54.280
And wouldn't it also be great if we got to
see Azrael again especially as Charlyne Yi

00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:57.500
was just fantastic in that role in season
3.

00:09:57.500 --> 00:10:02.740
The ending of Season 5 Part 1 seemingly reveals
that Charlie isn't a half-angel as we'd assumed

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:05.110
because he got sick with a fever and a cold.

00:10:05.110 --> 00:10:09.210
However, I think there's something else going
on here which caused Charlie's illness.

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:13.520
The clue is in the episode just before when
Amenadiel is talking to Linda about how content

00:10:13.520 --> 00:10:15.740
he is being a father and looking after Charlie.

00:10:15.740 --> 00:10:19.990
Linda agrees, but then tells him to enjoy
the moment while it lasts and adds that if

00:10:19.990 --> 00:10:24.080
they do a good job as parents, Charlie will
need them less and less every day.

00:10:24.080 --> 00:10:28.310
Amenadiel seems somewhat perturbed by this
realisation and given we know that Michael

00:10:28.310 --> 00:10:33.710
was trying to trigger his fears, could Amenadiel
have subconsciously accidentally made Charlie

00:10:33.710 --> 00:10:34.710
ill?

00:10:34.710 --> 00:10:39.290
Michael's fear mojo was powerful enough to
cause Amenadiel's time control powers to spiral

00:10:39.290 --> 00:10:43.110
out of control, so what else could they have
affected?

00:10:43.110 --> 00:10:47.270
My alternate theory on the cause of Charlie's
illness is that it's related to Amenadiel's

00:10:47.270 --> 00:10:52.930
misdiagnosis of Chlamydia by a doctor in Season
3, and I explain all that in my Season 5 Part

00:10:52.930 --> 00:10:54.200
1 Ending video.

00:10:54.200 --> 00:10:58.690
So, what do you think about these theories
for the show's final two seasons?

00:10:58.690 --> 00:11:02.120
And do you have any theories of your own on
how the series will end?

00:11:02.120 --> 00:11:04.290
Leave your thoughts in the comments below.

00:11:04.290 --> 00:11:07.890
Tap left to watch my next Lucifer video and
Season 5 playlist.

00:11:07.890 --> 00:11:10.529
Or tap right for another video you're sure
to like.

00:11:10.529 --> 00:11:13.870
And if you enjoyed this, a thumbs-up and a
share are hugely appreciated.

00:11:13.870 --> 00:11:15.960
Thanks for watching and see ya next time.

00:11:15.960 --> 00:11:17.250
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers!

